Okabe-Ito
----------

The Okabe-Ito color universal design palette is documented by Masataka Okabe
and Kei Ito at https://jfly.uni-koeln.de/color/. The distributed vector is the
exact `okabeito` object from khroma 1.17.0, with black moved to the end only in
scChromatic's priority order. khroma 1.17.0 is distributed under GPL (>= 3):
https://cran.r-project.org/src/contrib/khroma_1.17.0.tar.gz

Paul Tol
--------

Tol bright, vibrant, muted, and medium-contrast schemes are from Paul Tol,
"Colour Schemes", https://sronpersonalpages.nl/~pault/. The distributed
vectors are exact `bright`, `vibrant`, `muted`, and `mediumcontrast` objects
from khroma 1.17.0, which is distributed under GPL (>= 3):
https://cran.r-project.org/src/contrib/khroma_1.17.0.tar.gz

Only scChromatic's priority order for `tol_medium_contrast` is rearranged, to
place intended light/dark contrast pairs next to one another.

Glasbey
-------

The Glasbey palette is attributed to Glasbey CA, van der Heijden GWAM, Toh VFK,
and Gray AJ (2007), "Colour Displays for Categorical Images", Color Research
and Application 32:304-309, https://doi.org/10.1002/col.20327. The distributed
vector is the exact `glasbey` object from Polychrome 1.6.1. White is moved from
first to last only in scChromatic's priority order.

