scico
-----

scico_batlow, scico_lajolla, scico_vik, and scico_broc are interoperability
registry entries. scChromatic bundles the exact, unmodified 256-color
hexadecimal lookup tables returned by scico 1.5.0 (MIT), using Fabio Crameri's
Scientific colour maps 7.0.1 under CC BY 4.0:
https://cran.r-project.org/src/contrib/scico_1.5.0.tar.gz

The source lookup-table order and hexadecimal values are unchanged. Requests
for other output lengths are interpolated from these bundled tables and are
therefore adaptations by scChromatic. Attribute Fabio Crameri, cite Crameri,
Shephard, and Heron (2020), Nature Communications 11:5444, and link Scientific
colour maps 7.0.1 at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5501399. The complete CC BY
4.0 terms are installed at `licenses/CC-BY-4.0.txt`.

Generated scChromatic palettes
------------------------------

chromatic is regenerated for scChromatic as a nested, deterministic 40-color
sequence under GPL (>= 3). Runtime qualitative extension also belongs to
scChromatic. These colors are perceptually optimized and audited against normal,
deutan, protan, and tritan simulations; they are not claimed to be universally
color-blind safe. The generator is data-raw/generate-owned-palettes.R.

chromatic_balance is an 11-anchor diverging HCL palette generated with
colorspace::diverging_hcl() using hues 250 and 10, chroma 75, luminance 35 to
95, and power 1.1. It uses a neutral midpoint and was audited under normal,
deutan, protan, and tritan simulations. The colorspace package is BSD-3-Clause;
see Zeileis et al. (2020), Journal of Statistical Software 96(1):1-49.
